Z||000026||Galen||08-17-2001||09:04 PM||||Coco, you hit my latest argument right on the nose about the hippies not speaking english  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by annieL:<BR><B>People who park in handicapped spaces and are not handicapped.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif"> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Why should hadicapped ppl be treated any differantly than non handicapped person? Why should they get special parking? Thats not trating them or us equally. Its saying they are better than us becuz they are handicapped. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000027||annieL||08-17-2001||09:13 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Galen:<BR><B>Coco, you hit my latest argument right on the nose about the hippies not speaking english   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR> Why should handicapped ppl be treated any differently than non handicapped person? Why should they get special parking? Thats not trating them or us equally. Its saying they are better than us becuz they are handicapped. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>For some handicapped people there are legitimate reasons that there should be parking just for them. I work with disabled people and one guy is paralyzed on one side. Would you really expect him to walk a half a mile to get into a store? He wants  to be independent just like the rest of us but sometimes he needs a little help.<BR>||||reg||1
