Z||000030||rogergarrison||08-18-2001||12:17 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Dave Gunsul:<P><BR>2. Illinois construction!!! Can't they leave one friggin road alone for crying out loud??<P><BR>[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>didnt you hear, that how the efficient government does that. here too. would make sense to me to put all the men and equipment on one project and get it done really fast, then move on to the next. Instead if you want to be a government official, you have to block off 3/4 of all the roads in the area and put 3 men on each project. I once a couple years ago drove from columbus to cleveland on I-71 and there was at least 75 miles of hiway blocked off with barrels to one lane. whole way up I saw 2 guys with shovels sitting on a bridge rail, while cars and trucks went by bumper to bumper at 15mph.<P><p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 08-18-2001).]||||reg||1
