Z||000032||Galen||08-18-2001||02:47 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by annieL:<BR><B> For some handicapped people there are legitimate reasons that there should be parking just for them. I work with disabled people and one guy is paralyzed on one side. Would you really expect him to walk a half a mile to get into a store? He wants  to be independent just like the rest of us but sometimes he needs a little help.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I've got nothing against ppl that are legit about being disabled and need special help. But what erks me is ppl that are perfectly able and complain about being treated equally, but *****  like hell whenever someone is parked in a handicapped parking place. Cuz its theres and not ours, as if WE arn't as good as him. Even though we both are equal <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>Ray -  <A HREF="mailto:galen@ezrpg.com">galen@ezrpg.com</A>  - <A HREF="http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank>www.FieroLinks.f2s.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000033||annieL||08-18-2001||08:48 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Galen:<BR><B> I've got nothing against ppl that are legit about being disabled and need special help. But what erks me is ppl that are perfectly able and complain about being treated equally, but *****  like hell whenever someone is parked in a handicapped parking place. Cuz its theres and not ours, as if WE arn't as good as him. Even though we both are equal  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I agree with you 100% that people who are able should not park in handicapped spaces. I also work with another guy who does not have any physical disability (it's more developmental). If I take him out I WILL not park in handicapped spaces.<P>||||reg||1
